    "final_answer": ".spec.strategy.rollingUpdate.maxUnavailable\n- Meaning (from Deployment docs, RollingUpdate strategy → Max Unavailable): the maximum number of Pods that can be unavailable during an update.\n- Default value: 25% (if not specified, a default of 25% is used).\n\n.spec.strategy.rollingUpdate.maxSurge\n- Meaning (from Deployment docs, RollingUpdate strategy → Max Surge): the maximum number of Pods that can be created above the desired number of Pods during an update.\n- Default value: 25% (if not specified, a default of 25% is used).\n\n.spec.progressDeadlineSeconds\n- Meaning (from Deployment docs, section “Progress Deadline Seconds”): an optional field that specifies the number of seconds you want to wait for your Deployment to progress before the system reports that the Deployment has failed progressing (surfaced as a condition with type: Progressing, status: \"False\", and reason: ProgressDeadlineExceeded in the Deployment’s status). The Deployment controller will keep retrying the Deployment.\n- Default value: 600 seconds (\"This defaults to 600.\").\n\nAll meanings and defaults above are taken from the Kubernetes Deployments documentation field descriptions, not from example manifests, and percentage values and units are preserved as documented.",
